      "title": "Client Director",
      "description": "Client Director - London Business School Skip to main content This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. London Business School and our selected partners use cookies and similar technologies (together “cookies”) that are necessary to present this website, and to ensure you get the best experience of it.\n\n          If you consent to it, we will also use cookies for analytics purposes. See our Cookie Policy to read more about the cookies we set. You can withdraw and manage your consent at any time, by clicking “Manage cookies” at the bottom of each website page. Accept all cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Cookie preferences Select which cookies you accept On this site, we always set cookies that are strictly necessary, meaning they are necessary for the site to function properly. If you consent to it, we will also set other types of cookies. You can provide or withdraw your consent to the different types of cookies using the toggles below. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time, by clicking the link “Manage Cookies”, which is always available at the bottom of the site. To learn more about what the different types of cookies do, how your data is used when they are set etc, see our Cookie Policy . Strictly necessary These cookies are necessary to make the site work properly, and are always set when you visit the site. Vendors Teamtailor Analytics These cookies collect information to help us understand how the site is being used. Vendors Teamtailor Accept these cookies Decline all non-necessary cookies Career menu Work for us Employee Log in as employee Candidate Log in to Connect Homepage london.edu Share page Facebook X LinkedIn Mail Executive Education · London Business School, London · Hybrid Client Director Apply for this job Build substantial, profitable and enduring client relationships that help organisations transform through world-class executive education. The Role London Business School is looking for an experienced and commercially minded Client Director to join our Executive Education team on our London campus. This is a senior client relationship role focused on building, developing and managing high-quality relationships with large and medium-sized corporate clients. You will work in a matrix environment with learning specialists, account managers, faculty, marketing, bid and business operations colleagues to identify opportunities, shape solutions and secure new business. You will typically manage a portfolio of existing clients while also leading activity to win new client relationships and secure new business contracts. You will be accountable for the success and profitability of client relationships, from qualification and pitching through to contracting, mobilisation and delivery oversight. This is an opportunity to play a key role in growing London Business School’s Executive Education impact by connecting organisations with learning solutions that support their talent, leadership and executive development priorities. Main Responsibilities Lead and develop a portfolio of existing clients, building substantial, profitable and enduring relationships. Define and execute strategic account development plans to expand client relationships and identify new opportunities. Work as part of the client team to ensure learning solutions are delivered to agreed budget, quality and timeframe expectations. Drive a world-class client service, regularly reviewing quality and ensuring service meets client and stakeholder expectations. Anticipate and respond to complex client and stakeholder issues, resolving issues swiftly and escalating where appropriate. Qualify and scope new opportunities, developing responses to proposals and maximising the School’s likelihood of winning. Lead or contribute to commercial strategy for proposals in partnership with Bid and Business Operations teams. Engage with target clients aligned to agreed Custom Solutions targets by geography and industry. Develop specific outreach plans to identify and convert new business opportunities. Develop deep understanding of London Business School’s offer and apply this knowledge to create effective client and stakeholder solutions. Own the pipeline for your area, ensuring accurate forecasting and continuous development of new opportunities. Lead negotiation of high-value and non-standard contracts and agreements with clients and stakeholders. Use insight into client needs, financial targets and the School’s offer to ensure appropriate terms are agreed and delivered. Achieve or exceed revenue targets and contribute to wider team performance. Who We Are Looking For Significant experience in consultative sales and developing solutions with demanding clients. Excellent communication skills and the ability to develop and maintain client relationships at senior levels Strong negotiation, networking and influencing skills. The ability to manage multiple internal and external stakeholders and operate effectively with senior leaders. Experience of key account management and developing client relationships. Strong awareness of organisational activity, competitor schools and wider market context. The ability to scan the horizon, identify industry best practice and translate insight into future planning. Proven financial management skills and commercial acumen. Experience leading a team or operating in a senior leadership role. A collaborative, client-focused and solutions-oriented approach. Confidence working in a complex, matrix environment. Benefits You Can Enjoy Generous annual leave of 27 days plus extra days between Christmas and New Year USS pension, 14.5% employer contribution (in return for employee enrolment and contribution) Free onsite gym and swimming pool Amazing range of professional development to support your career path Enhanced cycle to work scheme Wellbeing offering to support your physical, mental and financial health At London Business School, we support Smart Working - a hybrid approach designed to help you achieve a healthy work-life balance while delivering the best outcomes for your role and the needs of our customers. All roles require a minimum of two days on campus each week to foster a vibrant, collaborative community. For this role specifically, you will be expected to be on campus 2 days per week. We operate with ‘core hours’ – 10:00-15:00 – to maximise opportunities for connection and collaboration across teams during the working day. Outside of these hours, you may still be required for meetings or collaboration based on your role and customer needs. Additionally, we offer Protected Time - a flexible, one-hour slot, within the working week dedicated to your learning and development, wellbeing, or focused, quiet work Why London Business School? London Business School; a global and vibrant business community based in three of the world’s most dynamic cities, London, Dubai and Riyadh. It’s where extraordinary minds and diverse perspectives connect, to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. We offer best in class hybrid learning to our students and participants, whilst creating a flexible, supportive and dynamic working environment for our people to excel in, whatever their location. Our commitment to driving inclusion and belonging We are a globally reaching institution, committed to creating tangible and sustainable change in driving inclusion & belonging within our School, education and society at large. We are dedicated to creating an environment where everyone in our community feels they belong and thrive. This is a key school priority, and we want everyone who joins LBS to feel respected, welcomed, and heard. Candidates needing sponsorship should assess their eligibility for a Certificate of Sponsorship by evaluating their circumstances against the relevant criteria before applying. Please note we start screening CVs and interviewing candidates from the start of a campaign. A successful candidate could progress to offer before the advertised closing date. We encourage you to apply as soon as possible if you are interested in any roles. View Job Description View London Business School Benefits Competitive Salary dependent upon experience Closing date: 5th October 2026 Department Executive Education Locations London Business School, London Remote status Hybrid About London Business School We exist to have a profound impact on the way the world does business and the way business impacts the world. London Business School’s academic strength and global outlook drives original and provocative business thinking. We challenge conventional wisdom, transform careers and empower our people to change the way the world does business. Apply for this job Executive Education · London Business School, London · Hybrid Client Director Loading application form Close modal Career site Work for us Data & privacy Manage cookies london.edu/ LinkedIn Employee login Candidate Connect login Already working at London Business School? Let’s recruit together and find your next colleague. Log in Applicant tracking system by Teamtailor"
    }
  },
